{"name":"Tiger Cub","hex":"#deae46","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tiger cub","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A young tiger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tiger_cub"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tiger Cub Developments Sherwood Ranger","blocks":[{"text":"The Tiger Cub Developments (TCD) Sherwood Ranger is a single engine, tandem two seat biplane microlight designed and built in the United Kingdom in the early 1990s. Kits were originally produced by TCD; later, design rights were acquired by The Light Aircraft Company Ltd (TLAC) who resumed kit production in 2009."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Sywell_070_-_Flickr_-_mick_-_Lumix.jpg/330px-Sywell_070_-_Flickr_-_mick_-_Lumix.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tiger_Cub_Developments_Sherwood_Ranger","wikidata":"Q7801396"},{"title":"Tiger Cub Economies","blocks":[{"text":"The Tiger Cub Economies collectively refer to the economies of the developing countries of Indonesia, Malaysia, the Philippines, Thailand and Vietnam, the five dominant countries in Southeast Asia."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Novos_Tigres_Asi%C3%A1ticos.png/330px-Novos_Tigres_Asi%C3%A1ticos.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tiger_Cub_Economies","wikidata":"Q1143093"},{"title":"Tiger","blocks":[{"text":"The tiger is a large cat and a member of the genus Panthera native to Asia. It has a powerful, muscular body with a large head and paws, a long tail and orange fur that fades to white in parts, with black, mostly vertical stripes. It is traditionally classified into nine subspecies, though some recognise only two subspecies, the mainland Asian tiger and the Sunda Islands tiger."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Bengal_tiger_%28Panthera_tigris_